    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0430" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg324"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-01-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill reports that the consul-general at Canton telegraphs him that the
                    Lienchou indemnity has been paid him by the viceroy, and that he is directing
                    the consul-general to remit it directly to the department. Mr. Rockhill hopes to
                    sign, at an early date, a legitimated settlement.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
